node_modules/
tools/*.png

# ---- real planning data must never be committed ----
# Everything the tool reads or writes is ignored by extension, because the
# rule cannot be undone once it is broken: a Genius report, a built book or
# a set of prints carries unit numbers, headcodes, staff names and real
# dates. It had been one `git add .` away - only `UNIT ORDER CHECK.csv` was
# named, while summary.pdf, out.csv, a books .zip and an allocations .xlsx
# were all trackable. `tools/order-check.mjs` even documents writing a file
# full of real formations into the working directory.
*.pdf
*.csv
*.xlsx
*.docx
*.doc
*.zip
# The weekend panel takes the prints as plain text too - a .txt saved out of
# Word, or the document copied and pasted - and that is the same real data.
# (Nothing tracked ends in .txt; `git ls-files '*.txt'` before adding one.)
*.txt
# …and the one document of that kind the repository does own
!HOW TO USE.docx

# Put anything real you need to keep beside the tool in here.
local/
